cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "passmcp-registry: a signed public scorecard of the MCP Registry's remote servers"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rousseau
    given-names: Sebastien
    email: sebastian.rousseau@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/sebastienrousseau/passmcp-registry"
url: "https://sebastienrousseau.com/passmcp-registry/"
abstract: >-
  A job that checks the remote servers listed in the official MCP Registry
  with a pinned passmcp release, read-only and without credentials, and
  publishes each result as an in-toto statement verified with
  passmcp-reporting and signed with cosign keyless. Results that would
  expose a vulnerability are withheld and queued, encrypted, for the
  server's owner under a 90-day disclosure policy; owners can opt out. The
  code is AGPL-3.0-only; the published scorecard and yearly reports are
  CC-BY-4.0.
keywords:
  - model-context-protocol
  - mcp
  - mcp-registry
  - scorecard
  - attestation
  - in-toto
  - golang
license: AGPL-3.0-only
version: 0.0.3
date-released: "2026-09-30"
